{
 "title": "A Volume-Price-Adjusted MACD Trading Strategy with Sensitivity Calibration for U.S. Equity Indices",
 "hypothesis": "H0 mu_new <= mu_old HA mu_new > mu_old for each pair Pair1 B vs A Pair2 C vs A Pair3 C vs B one-sided 5%",
 "data_sources": [
  "Yahoo Finance daily OHLCV SPY (S&P 500) QQQ (Nasdaq-100) DIA (Dow Jones Industrial Average)"
 ],
 "sample": "Daily market data (Open, High, Low, Close, Volume) for 3 U.S. equity index ETFs as proxies: S&P 500 SPY (market-cap-weighted, diversified large-cap, 11 sectors, high liquidity), Nasdaq-100 QQQ (market-cap-weighted, growth/tech-concentrated, high liquidity/high volatility), Dow Jones DIA (price-weighted, blue-chip, lower liquidity/lower volatility). Source Yahoo Finance. Daily trading frequency weekends/non-trading days excluded. Training calibration period: 2018 to 2022. Testing evaluation period: 2023-01-01 to 2026-02-28 out-of-sample. Strategy-specific index-specific lambda fixed from training applied to testing. No leverage, long-only fully invested min 1 share, execution next trading day open to avoid look-ahead. Costs applied.",
 "period_start": "2018",
 "period_end": "2026-02-28",
 "method": [
  "1 Data: Yahoo Finance daily OHLCV for SPY QQQ DIA. Sample 2018 to 2026-02-28 split training 2018-2022 (1,259 obs per instrument) testing 2023-01-01 to 2026-02-28 (791 obs per instrument). Exclude weekends/non-trading.",
  "2 Define SMA_t = 1/n sum_{i=0}^{n-1} P_{t-i} and EMA_t = alpha P_t + (1-alpha) EMA_{t-1} with alpha = 2/(n+1) n in trading days. Use n=12,26 for MACD.",
  "3 Traditional MACD: MACD_t = EMA12(P_t) - EMA26(P_t) ; Signal_t = EMA9(MACD_t) ; Hist_t = MACD_t - Signal_t ; P_t is closing price. Standard parameters (12,26,9).",
  "4 Trading rules: Baseline signal-line crossover Rule A: Buy if MACD_{t-1}<=Signal_{t-1} and MACD_t>Signal_t ; Sell if MACD_{t-1}>=Signal_{t-1} and MACD_t<Signal_t. In this study only Rule A used as benchmark. Zero-line and divergence excluded. Execution at next trading day opening price.",
  "5 Volume-price-adjusted price: Define N rolling window (N number past trading days, value not stated). For i in [t-N, t-1]: P*_t = sum P_i Volume_i sigma_i r_i / sum Volume_i. sigma_i = STD(P_i^{High}-P_i^{Low}) / P_i^{Close} normalized volatility. r_i = |P_i^{Close}-P_i^{Open}| / (P_i^{High}-P_i^{Low}) candlestick body ratio.",
  "6 VP-MACD indicator: VP-MACD_t = EMA12(P*_t) - EMA26(P*_t) ; Signal_t = EMA9(VP-MACD_t).",
  "7 Lambda-adjusted entry: lambda in (0.8,1) calibration range (practical not theoretical). Buy triggered when VP-MACD_{t-1} <= lambda Signal_{t-1} and VP-MACD_t > lambda Signal_t ; Sell if VP-MACD_{t-1} >= Signal_{t-1} and VP-MACD_t < Signal_t (no lambda on sell). Separate lambda optimized for Strategy B MACD+lambda (applied to traditional MACD) and Strategy C VP-MACD.",
  "8 Grid search calibration: lambda in [0.8,1.0] step 0.02 11 candidates per strategy per index using training data. Multi-criteria selection balancing win ratio, total PnL, PnL ratio, Sharpe, max drawdown, expectancy. Preference Sharpe + PnL ratio + expectancy without worsening DD. Result lambdas SPY 0.90/0.88 QQQ 0.84/0.98 DIA 0.92/0.86.",
  "9 Backtest simulation: Initialize V0=100,000 no leverage long-only fully invested min 1 share. Open on Buy close on Sell wait next Buy. Execute at next day open. Costs 4 bps one-way (3 bps trading + 1 bp slippage) both entry and exit => 8 bps round-trip per completed trade.",
  "10 Evaluation metrics definitions: Total Trades N buy-sell pairs ; Win Ratio Nwin/N ; PnL Ratio (Gains/Nwin)/(Losses/Nloss) ; Expectancy = WinRatio*Gbar - (1-WinRatio)*Lbar ; Total PnL = VT-V0 ; Sharpe = E[Rt]/sigma(Rt) * sqrt252 ; MDD = max_t (Peak_t - Value_t)/Peak_t with Peak_t = max_{s<=t} Value_s.",
  "11 Statistical tests on daily return differences testing period 791 obs per index. Hypotheses H0: mu_new <= mu_old HA: mu_new > mu_old per pair. Pair1 Strategy B vs A, Pair2 C vs A, Pair3 C vs B. Three complementary tests: (a) one-sided t-test mean difference >0, (b) HAC Newey-West adjusted t, (c) circular block bootstrap 1,000 resamples block length 5 non-parametric. Significance 5% p<0.05.",
  "12 Reporting: Tables 2-4 performance across 3 indices x 3 strategies testing period. Tables 5-6 t and Newey-West results. Figs 8-10 bootstrap distributions. Conclusions interpret economic and statistical improvements and trade-off selectivity vs frequency."
 ],
